WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
WebScaly. Sharper video, on your device.
Local enhancement for supported videos in Chrome.

00:03.000 --> 00:07.000
One frame. Two views.
Original and actual WebScaly Anime4K Quality output.

00:07.000 --> 00:10.000
Same frame. Equal crops and enlargement.
960×540 input to 1920×1080 output, 2× scale.

00:10.000 --> 00:13.000
Original AI-generated demonstration artwork.
640×360 input to 1920×1080 output, Automatic scale.

00:13.000 --> 00:15.000
Approve a website: Add this website, then Allow in Chrome.
The actual UI uses an isolated preapproved demo site.

00:15.000 --> 00:17.000
Turn on Enhancement.

00:17.000 --> 00:19.000
Choose Anime4K Quality.

00:19.000 --> 00:21.000
Enable Compare.

00:21.000 --> 00:25.000
Compare in the player.
Actual comparison UI, held captured frame.

00:25.000 --> 00:29.000
Set it. Save it.
Choose output size and save site preferences.
Spatial strength controls apply to Spatial Detail.

00:29.000 --> 00:34.000
Spatial Detail: sharpening and light denoise.
Anime4K: animation-oriented restore and upscale.
FSRCNNX: learned 2× upscaling.
Neural methods require supported WebGPU.

00:34.000 --> 00:38.000
Local GPU processing, on sites you approve.
The website keeps playback and audio.
No automatic WebScaly uploads.

00:38.000 --> 00:44.000
Free and open source. Available on the Chrome Web Store.
github.com/Lorcuz/WebScaly. Chrome 121+; compatibility varies.
